; gt.carp — what a Glamorous Toolkit session holds.
;
; The session a tool browses is what its entry loads, which is not always
; what the compiler builds. This entry is the compiler plus the parts that
; only make sense inside the tool: the session layer, and views over both,
; so a cell answering a type or a parsed module inspects as that thing.
;
;   (CarpProject onRoot: '<this repository>' entry: 'gt.carp') asBrowserTool
;
; The session host supplies the shared Carp view runtime before project
; files are loaded. These declarations reuse that host's view identities;
; notebook capture and remote Phlow transport belong to gt4carp.

(load "carp-session/carp-session.carp")
(load "views/compiler.carp")
(load "views/session.carp")
